  "contributors": "Christopher Daniel Pang supplied the PAL carried-frame question, RPL old/detail split, APCI comparison and the suggestion of 2663. Hearthline derived the two readings, finite inverse, signed jumps, perfect-square sampling and division-remainder criterion in Pang’s constructive program.",
  "formal_scope": "On the original Moebius divisions: collapsing reading, staircase reading, inverse cost four, pointwise remainder and capacity, exact difference, explicit late square sum and the half-unit bound on discarded early labels.",
  "analytic_scope": "The equivalence of RH to either one-sided subpower estimate on the normalized late square sum is a paper proof. The forward deduction uses the nonvanishing staircase multiplier and positivity at real abscissae. The converse uses the classical conditional Moebius estimate. The required all-head bound remains open.",
